{
 "set": "saturator-listening",
 "description": "m39-ad, the .saturator insert's new `oversampling` control. Every variant plays the IDENTICAL staccato pluck riff used by the transient-shaper and clipper demos, and every saturated variant uses the IDENTICAL settings (driveDb 30, mix 1, outputDb -3). The ONLY thing that changes is `oversampling`. \u26a0 HONEST CALIBRATION: on a 6272 Hz test tone the difference is 90.28 dB and unmissable; on MUSIC it is far smaller, because music's own harmonics mask the folded ones. Measure the difference rather than asserting it, and if it cannot be heard on a laptop speaker, say so - that is a real answer. \u26d4 The default is 1 (OFF) and that is NOT a quality judgement: this kind shipped long before the control existed, so existing projects must keep sounding exactly as they did.",
